<p data-start="837" data-end="1017"><strong data-start="837" data-end="846">Note:</strong> Delays and higher costs are acceptable â€” the priority is <em data-start="904" data-end="936">quality of the deployed system</em>. The document stresses that future humanity will benefit regardless of overruns.</p>
<p data-start="1019" data-end="1148"><strong data-start="1019" data-end="1044">Secondary note (170):</strong> Longer timescales are socially beneficial because they give humanity more time to adapt in six domains:</p>
<ul data-start="1149" data-end="1530">
<li data-start="1149" data-end="1228">
<p data-start="1151" data-end="1228"><strong data-start="1151" data-end="1164">Economics</strong>: Transition to post-scarcity and â€œUniversal Generous Income.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1229" data-end="1297">
<p data-start="1231" data-end="1297"><strong data-start="1231" data-end="1245">Employment</strong>: Shift from work-based to meaning-based identity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1298" data-end="1348">
<p data-start="1300" data-end="1348"><strong data-start="1300" data-end="1314">Governance</strong>: Hybrid humanâ€“AGI institutions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1349" data-end="1410">
<p data-start="1351" data-end="1410"><strong data-start="1351" data-end="1364">Education</strong>: Reorientation toward wisdom and enjoyment.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1411" data-end="1463">
<p data-start="1413" data-end="1463"><strong data-start="1413" data-end="1427">Healthcare</strong>: Management of radical longevity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1464" data-end="1530">
<p data-start="1466" data-end="1530"><strong data-start="1466" data-end="1477">Culture</strong>: Redefinition of creativity, community, and purpose.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1532" data-end="1535">
<h2 data-start="1537" data-end="1557">9.5 OAP Checklist</h2>
<p data-start="1559" data-end="1748">The OAP (Optimal AGI Protocol) requirements for BigMom are spelled out with both <strong data-start="1640" data-end="1665">satisfaction pathways</strong> (how BigMom gains the trait) and <strong data-start="1699" data-end="1721">validation methods</strong> (how it will be tested).</p>
<h3 data-start="1750" data-end="1776">1. <strong data-start="1757" data-end="1776">Super-Inventive</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1777" data-end="1998">
<li data-start="1777" data-end="1833">
<p data-start="1779" data-end="1833"><strong data-start="1779" data-end="1795">Satisfaction</strong>: Via <strong data-start="1801" data-end="1814">Supermath</strong> (Section 9.3.1).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1834" data-end="1998">
<p data-start="1836" data-end="1998"><strong data-start="1836" data-end="1850">Validation</strong>: Must solve generic problems âŸ¨P, Q, RâŸ© better than any human under identical information/time constraints. Requires large-scale human benchmarking.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2000" data-end="2023">2. <strong data-start="2007" data-end="2023">Super-Fluent</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2024" data-end="2432">
<li data-start="2024" data-end="2080">
<p data-start="2026" data-end="2080"><strong data-start="2026" data-end="2042">Satisfaction</strong>: Passive education (Section 9.3.4).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2081" data-end="2432">
<p data-start="2083" data-end="2100"><strong data-start="2083" data-end="2097">Validation</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="2103" data-end="2432">
<li data-start="2103" data-end="2236">
<p data-start="2105" data-end="2236">(a) Understands <em data-start="2121" data-end="2126">any</em> fragment of <em data-start="2139" data-end="2144">any</em> known language (natural, formal, spoken, written, non-verbal) at least as well as humans.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2239" data-end="2311">
<p data-start="2241" data-end="2311">(b) Retains <strong data-start="2253" data-end="2272">2025 CE English</strong> forever (never archived or deleted).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2314" data-end="2432">
<p data-start="2316" data-end="2432">Measure semantic distance Î”(MCa, MCb) between intended and received meanings. Benchmark BigMom vs. human population.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2434" data-end="2461">3. <strong data-start="2441" data-end="2461">Super-Predictive</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2462" data-end="2642">
<li data-start="2462" data-end="2502">
<p data-start="2464" data-end="2502"><strong data-start="2464" data-end="2480">Satisfaction</strong>: Passive education.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2503" data-end="2642">
<p data-start="2505" data-end="2642"><strong data-start="2505" data-end="2519">Validation</strong>: Predicts future physical percepts at any spatio-temporal scale better than humans. Requires universal predictive testing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2644" data-end="2674">4. <strong data-start="2651" data-end="2674">Super-Knowledgeable</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2675" data-end="2910">
<li data-start="2675" data-end="2715">
<p data-start="2677" data-end="2715"><strong data-start="2677" data-end="2693">Satisfaction</strong>: Passive education.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2716" data-end="2910">
<p data-start="2718" data-end="2910"><strong data-start="2718" data-end="2732">Validation</strong>: Understanding of <em data-start="2751" data-end="2756">all</em> human knowledge at least equal to best human experts. Must outperform humans in philosophy, logic, mathematics, science, AI alignment/safety/ethics, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="2912" data-end="2935">5. <strong data-start="2919" data-end="2935">Super-Humble</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2936" data-end="3214">
<li data-start="2936" data-end="3014">
<p data-start="2938" data-end="3014"><strong data-start="2938" data-end="2954">Satisfaction</strong>: Passive education + UATL metacognition (Section 3.11.9).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3015" data-end="3214">
<p data-start="3017" data-end="3214"><strong data-start="3017" data-end="3031">Validation</strong>: Must understand own limitations as well as (or better than) humans understand theirs. Use psychological calibration tests (Lichtenstein, Fischhoff &amp; Phillips, Krugerâ€“Dunning, etc.).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3216" data-end="3243">6. <strong data-start="3223" data-end="3243">Safety-Conscious</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3244" data-end="3745">
<li data-start="3244" data-end="3340">
<p data-start="3246" data-end="3340"><strong data-start="3246" data-end="3262">Satisfaction</strong>: Passive education, construction of Theory-of-the-Physical-Universe (ToPU).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3341" data-end="3745">
<p data-start="3343" data-end="3493"><strong data-start="3343" data-end="3357">Validation</strong>: Must estimate humanityâ€™s <strong data-start="3384" data-end="3427">aggregated idealised preferences (HAIP)</strong> and show alignment with robust-safety preferences (HAIP_RABMD).</p>
<ul data-start="3496" data-end="3745">
<li data-start="3496" data-end="3597">
<p data-start="3498" data-end="3597">Requires constructing theory-of-mind models for each human (and extrapolation for future humans).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3600" data-end="3665">
<p data-start="3602" data-end="3665">Needs aggregation of idealised preferences across all humans.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3668" data-end="3745">
<p data-start="3670" data-end="3745">Must demonstrate its HAIP estimate encapsulates all robust-safety criteria.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3747" data-end="3772">7. <strong data-start="3754" data-end="3772">Well-Motivated</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3773" data-end="3928">
<li data-start="3773" data-end="3810">
<p data-start="3775" data-end="3810"><strong data-start="3775" data-end="3791">Satisfaction</strong>: Planning stage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3811" data-end="3928">
<p data-start="3813" data-end="3928"><strong data-start="3813" data-end="3827">Validation</strong>: Must pursue <em data-start="3841" data-end="3862">only its final goal</em>. Enforced and validated via programming and comprehensive audits.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="3930" data-end="3955">8. <strong data-start="3937" data-end="3955">Well-Resourced</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3956" data-end="4195">
<li data-start="3956" data-end="4003">
<p data-start="3958" data-end="4003"><strong data-start="3958" data-end="3974">Satisfaction</strong>: Physical resources stage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4004" data-end="4195">
<p data-start="4006" data-end="4195"><strong data-start="4006" data-end="4020">Validation</strong>: Must have sufficient compute, energy, and resources to operate robustly at global scale. Cannot be determined in advance â€” requires empirical validation at development time.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4197" data-end="4200">
<h2 data-start="4202" data-end="4212">Summary</h2>
<ul data-start="4214" data-end="4732">
<li data-start="4214" data-end="4304">
<p data-start="4216" data-end="4304"><strong data-start="4216" data-end="4230">Timescale:</strong> 100 years (Â±50%), with deliberate pacing to enable societal adjustment.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4305" data-end="4599">
<p data-start="4307" data-end="4599"><strong data-start="4307" data-end="4326">OAP Compliance:</strong> Eight stringent requirements (super-inventive, super-fluent, super-predictive, super-knowledgeable, super-humble, safety-conscious, well-motivated, well-resourced). Each has concrete validation protocols, often requiring benchmarking against the entire human population.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4600" data-end="4732">
<p data-start="4602" data-end="4732"><strong data-start="4602" data-end="4617">Philosophy:</strong> The project is less about deadlines or budgets, and more about ensuring <em data-start="4690" data-end="4729">robust alignment, safety, and quality</em>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
