3.71685 11.4352 3.83766 11.2176 3.97765 11.0127L4.15343 10.7783C4.34386 10.5462 4.58164 10.312 4.90538 9.98829L11.1964 3.6963L11.3312 3.56837ZM5.84581 10.9287C5.49664 11.2779 5.31252 11.4634 5.18663 11.6162L5.07531 11.7627C4.98188 11.8995 4.90151 12.0448 4.83507 12.1963L4.77355 12.3506C4.73321 12.4607 4.70242 12.5761 4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="ce97c0d7-572d-44f7-a2ea-b88fba006b38" data-testid="conversation-turn-10" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="ce97c0d7-572d-44f7-a2ea-b88fba006b38" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="360">Thanks for pasting the <strong data-start="23" data-end="39">front matter</strong> of Aaron Turnerâ€™s paper. Now that we can see the title, abstract, and framing in one place, the critique sharpens even more â€” because the <em data-start="178" data-end="195">Abstract itself</em> contains most of the structural flaws youâ€™ve already identified. Let me unpack how this introduction sets up the problems that later show up in the OAP checklist.</p>
<hr data-start="362" data-end="365">
<h2 data-start="367" data-end="422">1. The Problem of Undefined Core Concepts (TTQ, OAP)</h2>
<p data-start="424" data-end="563">The abstract introduces <strong data-start="448" data-end="455">TTQ</strong> (the final goal) and <strong data-start="477" data-end="484">OAP</strong> (Outer Alignment Precondition) as if they were well-defined constructs. But:</p>
<ul data-start="565" data-end="996">
<li data-start="565" data-end="776">
<p data-start="567" data-end="776"><strong data-start="567" data-end="574">TTQ</strong> is described only in natural language: â€œstrives to maximise the net benefit of AGI for all humanity, without favouring any subset thereof.â€ This is an <em data-start="726" data-end="750">aspirational statement</em>, not a computable goal.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="777" data-end="996">
<p data-start="779" data-end="996"><strong data-start="779" data-end="786">OAP</strong> is defined circularly: â€œif a goal-less superintelligent agent satisfies OAP, then TTQ works as intended.â€ This simply restates the alignment problem in different terms: <em data-start="956" data-end="994">if alignment works, alignment works.</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="998" data-end="1200">This is the paperâ€™s central act of <strong data-start="1033" data-end="1047">handwaving</strong>: it imports the unsolved difficulty of defining human-aligned objectives into an undefined placeholder (OAP), which is then assumed to be satisfiable.</p>
<hr data-start="1202" data-end="1205">
<h2 data-start="1207" data-end="1262">2. Contradictory Claims of Implementation-Neutrality</h2>
<p data-start="1264" data-end="1365">The title promises an <strong data-start="1286" data-end="1321">Implementation-Neutral Solution</strong>, but the abstract itself undermines this:</p>
<ul data-start="1367" data-end="1663">
<li data-start="1367" data-end="1539">
<p data-start="1369" data-end="1539">After saying OAP applies â€œirrespective of the specific technology,â€ the author immediately proposes a <strong data-start="1471" data-end="1527">â€œtentative neurosymbolic non-LLM-basedâ€ architecture</strong> (BigMom).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1540" data-end="1663">
<p data-start="1542" data-end="1663">This is not neutral. It is a commitment to a particular paradigm (neurosymbolic AI) and an exclusion of another (LLMs).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1665" data-end="1785">The contradiction is obvious even before Section 9.4â€“9.5: neutrality is claimed rhetorically but violated technically.</p>
<hr data-start="1787" data-end="1790">
<h2 data-start="1792" data-end="1846">3. Aspirational Language Without Technical Pathways</h2>
<p data-start="1848" data-end="1914">The abstract repeatedly uses maximally aspirational descriptors:</p>
<ul data-start="1916" data-end="1998">
<li data-start="1916" data-end="1939">
<p data-start="1918" data-end="1939">â€œMaximally-alignedâ€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1940" data-end="1965">
<p data-start="1942" data-end="1965">â€œMaximally-validatedâ€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1966" data-end="1998">
<p data-start="1968" data-end="1998">â€œMaximally-superintelligentâ€</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2000" data-end="2036">But none of these are grounded in:</p>
<ul data-start="2037" data-end="2215">
<li data-start="2037" data-end="2090">
<p data-start="2039" data-end="2090">A <strong data-start="2041" data-end="2051">metric</strong> (what counts as maximally aligned?).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2091" data-end="2151">
<p data-start="2093" data-end="2151">A <strong data-start="2095" data-end="2120">verification protocol</strong> (how is maximality tested?).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2152" data-end="2215">
<p data-start="2154" data-end="2215">A <strong data-start="2156" data-end="2180">construction pathway</strong> (how is maximality engineered?).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2217" data-end="2437">The text asserts the existence of a <strong data-start="2253" data-end="2274">Gold-Standard AGI</strong> as if describing it were sufficient to make it real. This is a classic hallmark of vision papers that mistake <em data-start="2385" data-end="2406">naming the property</em> for <em data-start="2411" data-end="2434">specifying the method</em>.</p>
<hr data-start="2439" data-end="2442">
<h2 data-start="2444" data-end="2515">4. The Hidden Value Judgment: â€œWithout Favouring Any Subset Thereofâ€</h2>
<p data-start="2517" data-end="2649">The phrase â€œstrives to maximise the net benefit of AGI for all humanity, without favouring any subset thereofâ€ sounds benign, but:</p>
<ul data-start="2651" data-end="3277">
<li data-start="2651" data-end="2881">
<p data-start="2653" data-end="2881"><strong data-start="2653" data-end="2673">Philosophically:</strong> It presupposes that there exists a single aggregation of values that does not favour any group â€” which is contested by nearly every major ethical theory (e.g., utilitarianism, Rawlsian justice, pluralism).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2882" data-end="3112">
<p data-start="2884" data-end="3112"><strong data-start="2884" data-end="2900">Technically:</strong> It assumes an AGI can infer â€œidealised preferencesâ€ for both living and <em data-start="2973" data-end="2981">future</em> humans, under conditions of perfect rationality, full information, and freedom. This is not just unsolved, it may be incoherent.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3113" data-end="3277">
<p data-start="3115" data-end="3277"><strong data-start="3115" data-end="3131">Politically:</strong> It ignores the reality that alignment is always contested; any aggregation procedure encodes choices about weighting, fairness, and compromise.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3279" data-end="3401">The abstract treats this <em data-start="3304" data-end="3321">central dilemma</em> as though it were a settled precondition, which is a deep form of handwaving.</p>
<hr data-start="3403" data-end="3406">
<h2 data-start="3408" data-end="3444">5. The Architecture Contradiction</h2>
<p data-start="3446" data-end="3475">Finally, the abstract says:</p>
<blockquote data-start="3477" data-end="3622">
<p data-start="3479" data-end="3622">â€œIn order to demonstrate their feasibility, we briefly outline a tentative neurosymbolic non-LLM-based OAP-compliant cognitive architecture.â€</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="3624" data-end="3926">But if the entire contribution rests on defining TTQ and OAP, then <em data-start="3691" data-end="3742">demonstrating feasibility through an architecture</em> presupposes those definitions are already in place. It inverts the logical order: the architecture cannot be shown to be OAP-compliant if OAP itself has never been formally defined.</p>
<hr data-start="3928" data-end="3931">
<h2 data-start="3933" data-end="3945">Synthesis</h2>
<p data-start="3947" data-end="4009">The <strong data-start="3951" data-end="3970">Abstract itself</strong> is already a microcosm of the flaws:</p>
<ol data-start="4011" data-end="4457">
<li data-start="4011" data-end="4070">
<p data-start="4014" data-end="4070"><strong data-start="4014" data-end="4028">Vagueness:</strong> TTQ and OAP are undefined placeholders.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4071" data-end="4151">
<p data-start="4074" data-end="4151"><strong data-start="4074" data-end="4092">Contradiction:</strong> Implementation neutrality is promised but not delivered.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4152" data-end="4241">
<p data-start="4155" data-end="4241"><strong data-start="4155" data-end="4183">Aspirational maximalism:</strong> Uses â€œmaximalâ€ descriptors without metrics or pathways.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4242" data-end="4367">
<p data-start="4245" data-end="4367"><strong data-start="4245" data-end="4274">Philosophical handwaving:</strong> Treats the aggregation of all human values (including future peopleâ€™s) as straightforward.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4368" data-end="4457">
<p data-start="4371" data-end="4457"><strong data-start="4371" data-end="4387">Circularity:</strong> Proposes an â€œOAP-compliantâ€ architecture without ever defining OAP.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="4459" data-end="4665">In short: the abstract is rhetorically powerful but technically empty. It positions BigMom as a â€œGold-Standard AGIâ€ while leaving every critical concept either undefined, contradictory, or handwaved away.</p>
<hr data-start="4667" data-end="4670">
<p data-start="4672" data-end="4991" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to <strong data-start="4693" data-end="4733">draft a one-page academic commentary</strong> (the kind youâ€™d see in <em data-start="4757" data-end="4771">AI &amp; Society</em> or <em data-start="4775" data-end="4800">Philosophy &amp; Technology</em>) that summarizes these flaws and positions the paper as an example of <em data-start="4871" data-end="4932">alignment by rhetoric rather than alignment by construction</em>? That would let you use it as a standalone critical piece.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.04