<p data-start="183" data-end="212">From the abstract you pasted:</p>
<blockquote data-start="214" data-end="415">
<p data-start="216" data-end="415"><em data-start="216" data-end="415">â€œwe formulate a final goal <strong data-start="244" data-end="251">TTQ</strong> and corresponding Outer Alignment Precondition OAP such that, if goal-less superintelligent agent <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^-</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7713em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7713em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">âˆ’</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> satisfies OAP â€¦ then final goal TTQ works as intended â€¦â€</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="417" data-end="455">There are two things happening here:</p>
<ol data-start="457" data-end="1205">
<li data-start="457" data-end="791">
<p data-start="460" data-end="497"><strong data-start="460" data-end="495">Stylistic mimicry of formalism.</strong></p>
<ul data-start="501" data-end="791">
<li data-start="501" data-end="609">
<p data-start="503" data-end="609">TTQ is typeset like a mathematical object (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="bold">T</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">T</mi><mi mathvariant="bold">Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{TTQ}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8805em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf">TTQ</span></span></span></span></span>), as if it were a formally defined quantity.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="613" data-end="694">
<p data-start="615" data-end="694">But nowhere is â€œTTQâ€ expanded into words or derived from an existing concept.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="698" data-end="791">
<p data-start="700" data-end="791">It functions rhetorically, giving the impression of rigor without supplying a definition.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="793" data-end="1205">
<p data-start="796" data-end="818"><strong data-start="796" data-end="816">Probable intent.</strong></p>
<ul data-start="822" data-end="1205">
<li data-start="822" data-end="936">
<p data-start="824" data-end="936">Based on context, TTQ seems to mean <em data-start="860" data-end="886">the final goal statement</em> â€” the thing that the agent will forever pursue.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="940" data-end="1134">
<p data-start="942" data-end="1134">It might stand for something like <strong data-start="976" data-end="999">â€œThe True Questionâ€</strong> or <strong data-start="1003" data-end="1033">â€œTop-Level Terminal Questâ€</strong> or <strong data-start="1037" data-end="1069">â€œTargeted Terminal Quantityâ€</strong> (Turnerâ€™s style suggests he likes acronym-heavy formulations).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1138" data-end="1205">
<p data-start="1140" data-end="1205">But since it is never spelled out, the reader is left guessing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1207" data-end="1634">So youâ€™re right to feel uncertain: <strong data-start="1242" data-end="1320">TTQ is not actually an established acronym â€” itâ€™s an invented placeholder.</strong> The paper treats it as though it were the mathematically precise definition of the final goal, but itâ€™s never defined. This is exactly the handwaving problem you flagged: the author replaces the hardest part of outer alignment (â€œwhat is the goal?â€) with a three-letter acronym and assumes the problem is solved.</p>
<hr data-start="1636" data-end="1639">
<p data-start="1641" data-end="2010" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to dig into Turnerâ€™s earlier writings and see if heâ€™s ever used â€œTTQâ€ elsewhere (to confirm what he thinks it stands for), or would you prefer I help you coin a precise alternative definition that exposes the weakness â€” e.g., rewrite the abstract with TTQ replaced by something clearer like <em data-start="1950" data-end="1982">FGS (Final Goal Specification)</em> so the gap becomes obvious?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C