l-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="86">Excellent â€” the <strong data-start="16" data-end="32">Introduction</strong> youâ€™ve pasted clarifies the situation with <strong data-start="76" data-end="83">TTQ</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="88" data-end="127">Hereâ€™s the key passage (Section 1.5):</p>
<blockquote data-start="129" data-end="559">
<p data-start="131" data-end="559"><em data-start="131" data-end="557">â€œâ€¦we then apply the same approach to the problem of designing and building an aligned and validated superintelligent agent: (1) formulating the final goal (<strong data-start="288" data-end="295">TTQ</strong>), (2) working backwards from that final goal to identify the desired properties (<strong data-start="377" data-end="384">OAP</strong>) we require a goal-less superintelligent agent to possess, (3) designing, building, and validating a goal-less superintelligent agent, and (4) plugging in the final goal.â€</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="561" data-end="566">So:</p>
<ul data-start="568" data-end="1108">
<li data-start="568" data-end="663">
<p data-start="570" data-end="663"><strong data-start="570" data-end="604">TTQ is not a standard acronym.</strong> It is the authorâ€™s shorthand label for â€œthe final goal.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="664" data-end="860">
<p data-start="666" data-end="860">It doesnâ€™t expand to something like <em data-start="702" data-end="728">Target Terminal Quantity</em> or <em data-start="732" data-end="753">True Terminal Quest</em>. Itâ€™s just a symbol â€” a placeholder for â€œthe specification of the final goal we want the AGI to pursue.â€</p>
</li>
<li data-start="861" data-end="1108">
<p data-start="863" data-end="898">Its role is symmetrical with OAP:</p>
<ul data-start="901" data-end="1108">
<li data-start="901" data-end="973">
<p data-start="903" data-end="973">TTQ = <em data-start="909" data-end="971">what the agent ultimately pursues (final goal specification)</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="976" data-end="1108">
<p data-start="978" data-end="1108">OAP = <em data-start="984" data-end="1106">the preconditions required so that, once TTQ is added to a goal-less agent, that agent pursues it safely and as intended</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1110" data-end="1331">The problem is that while the notation gives an impression of precision, <strong data-start="1183" data-end="1225">TTQ is never formally defined anywhere</strong> in the introduction (and seemingly not in the abstract either). Instead, itâ€™s described aspirationally:</p>
<ul data-start="1333" data-end="1511">
<li data-start="1333" data-end="1449">
<p data-start="1335" data-end="1449"><em data-start="1335" data-end="1436">â€œstrives to maximise the net benefit of AGI for all humanity, without favouring any subset thereofâ€</em> (Abstract)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1450" data-end="1511">
<p data-start="1452" data-end="1511"><em data-start="1452" data-end="1489">â€œâ€¦formulating the final goal (TTQ)â€</em> (Introduction, 1.5)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1513" data-end="1784">But this is exactly the handwaving you noticed: <strong data-start="1561" data-end="1706">the hardest part of alignment is translating â€œmaximise the net benefit of AGI for all humanityâ€ into a computable, unambiguous specification.</strong> Calling that TTQ doesnâ€™t solve the problem; it just hides it under a label.</p>
<hr data-start="1786" data-end="1789">
<h3 data-start="1791" data-end="1802">TL;DR</h3>
<ul data-start="1803" data-end="2131">
<li data-start="1803" data-end="1862">
<p data-start="1805" data-end="1862"><strong data-start="1805" data-end="1831">TTQ = â€œthe final goalâ€</strong> in the authorâ€™s terminology.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1863" data-end="1919">
<p data-start="1865" data-end="1919">It is not a standard acronym; itâ€™s a symbolic label.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1920" data-end="1980">
<p data-start="1922" data-end="1980">Its definition is vague and aspirational, not technical.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1981" data-end="2131">
<p data-start="1983" data-end="2131">The introduction confirms that TTQ is meant to be the counterpart to OAP, but does not resolve the core problem of how TTQ is actually formalized.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2133" data-end="2136">
<p data-start="2138" data-end="2517" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to <strong data-start="2156" data-end="2207">trace through the rest of the paperâ€™s structure</strong> (at least from the introduction) to map exactly where TTQ is invoked and whether it ever receives a real mathematical definition â€” or shall I focus on helping you <em data-start="2371" data-end="2409">recast TTQ into a more rigorous form</em> (e.g., comparing it to Russellâ€™s Cooperative IRL â€œvalue functionâ€ or Christianoâ€™s â€œidealized preferencesâ€)?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.333