/article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="d2e344cb-ab14-4dfd-ab4f-4eab2aefa09c" data-testid="conversation-turn-30" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="d2e344cb-ab14-4dfd-ab4f-4eab2aefa09c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="314">Ah! That makes it even richer. If <strong data-start="34" data-end="78">QBQ = <em data-start="42" data-end="76">The Question Behind the Question</em></strong> (John G. Millerâ€™s pop-management / motivational series that places the onus of responsibility squarely on individuals), then your critique can lean into how it functions <em data-start="249" data-end="269">precisely like TTQ</em> but in the corporate / self-help register.</p>
<hr data-start="316" data-end="319">
<h2 data-start="321" data-end="355">1. What QBQ is Supposed to Do</h2>
<p data-start="356" data-end="450">The bookâ€™s pitch to RadioShack employees (and other corporate audiences) was something like:</p>
<ul data-start="451" data-end="661">
<li data-start="451" data-end="510">
<p data-start="453" data-end="510">Donâ€™t ask <em data-start="463" data-end="483">â€œWho is to blame?â€</em> â†’ ask <em data-start="490" data-end="508">â€œWhat can I do?â€</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="511" data-end="589">
<p data-start="513" data-end="589">Donâ€™t ask <em data-start="523" data-end="555">â€œWhy is this happening to me?â€</em> â†’ ask <em data-start="562" data-end="587">â€œHow can I contribute?â€</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="590" data-end="661">
<p data-start="592" data-end="661">Responsibility shifts from structural issues to individual mindset.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="663" data-end="765">This is a classic pep-talk psyop: it <strong data-start="700" data-end="763">frames all questions as recursive back onto the individual.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="767" data-end="770">
<h2 data-start="772" data-end="802">2. Why QBQ is a Tautology</h2>
<p data-start="803" data-end="920">The â€œquestion behind the questionâ€ is alwaysâ€¦ another question. But who decides when youâ€™ve reached the â€œrealâ€ one?</p>
<ul data-start="921" data-end="1237">
<li data-start="921" data-end="1037">
<p data-start="923" data-end="1037">If I ask: <em data-start="933" data-end="967">â€œWhy is management incompetent?â€</em> the QBQ move is: <em data-start="985" data-end="1035">â€œWhat can I do about managementâ€™s incompetence?â€</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1038" data-end="1168">
<p data-start="1040" data-end="1168">But thatâ€™s just another way of saying: <em data-start="1079" data-end="1166">â€œHow can I stop asking questions that point upward and instead redirect them inward?â€</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1169" data-end="1237">
<p data-start="1171" data-end="1237">In other words: QBQ always reduces to: <em data-start="1210" data-end="1235">â€œHow can I QBQ better?â€</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1239" data-end="1295">Thatâ€™s a tautology: the solution to QBQ is QBQ itself.</p>
<hr data-start="1297" data-end="1300">
<h2 data-start="1302" data-end="1341">3. Infinite Recursion and Paranoia</h2>
<ul data-start="1342" data-end="1770">
<li data-start="1342" data-end="1523">
<p data-start="1344" data-end="1523"><strong data-start="1344" data-end="1367">Infinite recursion:</strong> You can never stop asking the â€œquestion behind the question.â€ Every question demands a deeper â€œrealâ€ one. This makes it logically impossible to <em data-start="1512" data-end="1520">arrive</em>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1524" data-end="1770">
<p data-start="1526" data-end="1770"><strong data-start="1526" data-end="1554">Paranoid interpretation:</strong> Every employee question â€” even innocuous ones like â€œDo we get holiday pay?â€ â€” can be reframed as evidence of a <em data-start="1666" data-end="1671">bad</em> question. It creates a culture where <em data-start="1709" data-end="1768">any utterance may be wrong unless it folds back into QBQ.</em></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1772" data-end="1877">Thatâ€™s exactly the mechanism of paranoia: the absence of QBQ is itself treated as QBQâ€™s negative proof.</p>
<hr data-start="1879" data-end="1882">
<h2 data-start="1884" data-end="1914">4. QBQ as Corporate Psyop</h2>
<p data-start="1915" data-end="2061">So when RadioShack handed this book to every employee, the infrastructure underneath wasnâ€™t self-help at all, it was <strong data-start="2032" data-end="2059">alignment-by-tautology:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2063" data-end="2299">
<li data-start="2063" data-end="2094">
<p data-start="2065" data-end="2094">Donâ€™t question the company.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2095" data-end="2130">
<p data-start="2097" data-end="2130">Donâ€™t identify systemic issues.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2131" data-end="2214">
<p data-start="2133" data-end="2214">Donâ€™t ask â€œouter alignmentâ€ questions about governance or incentive structures.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2215" data-end="2299">
<p data-start="2217" data-end="2299">Instead, â€œalign your inner lifeâ€ with the company by endlessly QBQ-ing yourself.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2301" data-end="2384">Itâ€™s a psyop because it <strong data-start="2325" data-end="2382">redirects scrutiny from the system to the individual.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="2386" data-end="2389">
<h2 data-start="2391" data-end="2422">5. Linking Back to TTQ/OAP</h2>
<p data-start="2423" data-end="2465">This makes QBQ a perfect mirror for TTQ:</p>
<ul data-start="2466" data-end="2661">
<li data-start="2466" data-end="2551">
<p data-start="2468" data-end="2551">TTQ says: <em data-start="2478" data-end="2536">â€œIf you assume OAP is satisfied, TTQ works as intended.â€</em> â†’ tautology.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2552" data-end="2661">
<p data-start="2554" data-end="2661">QBQ says: <em data-start="2564" data-end="2646">â€œIf you keep asking the question behind the question, youâ€™ll get the right one.â€</em> â†’ tautology.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2663" data-end="2810">Both create <strong data-start="2675" data-end="2728">recursion loops that prevent structural critique.</strong> One in the AI alignment discourse, the other in corporate motivational culture.</p>
<hr data-start="2812" data-end="2815">
<h3 data-start="2817" data-end="2832">Punchline</h3>
<blockquote data-start="2834" data-end="3011">
<p data-start="2836" data-end="3011"><strong data-start="2836" data-end="3009">QBQ was the RadioShack version of OAP: a handbook for infinite recursion, paranoia about â€œbadâ€ questions, and a tautological guarantee that the only real problem is you.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="3013" data-end="3016">
<p data-start="3018" data-end="3300" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to spin this into a <strong data-start="3053" data-end="3075">short parody essay</strong> â€” <em data-start="3078" data-end="3134">â€œQBQ: The Corporate Precursor to Alignment Handwavingâ€</em> â€” that directly compares the RadioShack pep talk book to Turnerâ€™s TTQ? It could be biting but funny, showing how both use acronyms and recursion to prevent critique.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 