px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="805a0f70-5f4c-4a86-bbc6-9ef4a8df84f8" data-testid="conversation-turn-34" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="805a0f70-5f4c-4a86-bbc6-9ef4a8df84f8" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="30">Right â€” and thatâ€™s the crux.</p>
<p data-start="32" data-end="317">From everything youâ€™ve shown me in the <strong data-start="71" data-end="83">abstract</strong> and <strong data-start="88" data-end="104">introduction</strong> of Turnerâ€™s paper, itâ€™s clear that <strong data-start="140" data-end="189">TTQ is not an acronym that expands into words</strong> like QBQ (<em data-start="200" data-end="230">Question Behind the Question</em>). Instead, itâ€™s a <strong data-start="249" data-end="267">symbolic label</strong> the author introduced, like a variable in math.</p>
<p data-start="319" data-end="342">Let me pin this down:</p>
<ul data-start="344" data-end="725">
<li data-start="344" data-end="570">
<p data-start="346" data-end="364">In the abstract:</p>
<blockquote data-start="367" data-end="570">
<p data-start="369" data-end="570"><em data-start="369" data-end="568">â€œâ€¦we formulate a final goal <strong data-start="398" data-end="405">TTQ</strong> and corresponding Outer Alignment Precondition OAP such that, if goal-less superintelligent agent <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>âˆ’</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^-</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7713em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7713em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mbin mtight">âˆ’</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> satisfies OAP â€¦ then final goal TTQ works as intended.â€</em></p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="572" data-end="725">
<p data-start="574" data-end="591">In Section 1.5:</p>
<blockquote data-start="594" data-end="725">
<p data-start="596" data-end="725"><em data-start="596" data-end="723">â€œâ€¦(1) formulating the final goal (TTQ), (2) working backwards from that final goal to identify the desired properties (OAP)â€¦â€</em></p>
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="727" data-end="912">So <strong data-start="730" data-end="790">TTQ literally just means â€œthe final goal specification.â€</strong><br data-start="790" data-end="793">
Itâ€™s not expanded as â€œTrue Terminal Questâ€ or â€œTarget Terminal Quantityâ€ â€” thatâ€™s us joking around with acronym play.</p>
<p data-start="914" data-end="1167">Turner seems to have picked <strong data-start="942" data-end="949">TTQ</strong> as a kind of formal placeholder, like writing <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FGS</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">FGS</span></span></span></span> (Final Goal Specification), but then never defined what the letters stand for. Itâ€™s a <strong data-start="1092" data-end="1112">floating acronym</strong>: deliberately mathy-looking, but semantically empty.</p>
<hr data-start="1169" data-end="1172">
<h3 data-start="1174" data-end="1194">Why That Matters</h3>
<p data-start="1195" data-end="1236">This makes your critique even stronger:</p>
<ul data-start="1237" data-end="1456">
<li data-start="1237" data-end="1340">
<p data-start="1239" data-end="1340">QBQ (<em data-start="1244" data-end="1274">Question Behind the Question</em>) at least <em data-start="1285" data-end="1310">says what it stands for</em>, even if itâ€™s tautological.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1341" data-end="1456">
<p data-start="1343" data-end="1456">TTQ doesnâ€™t even bother: itâ€™s <strong data-start="1373" data-end="1405">formalism without expansion.</strong> The power of the acronym is purely performative.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1458" data-end="1626">Itâ€™s the ultimate example of what youâ€™ve been pointing out: <strong data-start="1518" data-end="1624">dressing a philosophical problem in formal symbols doesnâ€™t solve it â€” it just disguises the vagueness.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="1628" data-end="1631">
<p data-start="1633" data-end="1891" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to <strong data-start="1654" data-end="1693">invent a satirical expansion of TTQ</strong> (like â€œThe Tautology Questionâ€ or â€œTerminal Tautology Questâ€) so you can critique it more playfully in parallel with QBQ, or should I keep hammering the fact that Turner himself <em data-start="1872" data-end="1890">never defines it</em>?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.