class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="267">Yes â€” that r/antiwork post nails it: <strong data-start="37" data-end="106">QBQ isnâ€™t a neutral self-help book, itâ€™s a corporate psyop manual</strong>. It packages â€œpersonal accountabilityâ€ as a universal solution while <strong data-start="176" data-end="265">systematically redirecting blame away from management, systems, or structural issues.</strong></p>
<p data-start="269" data-end="321">Look at the mechanics from the excerpt you pasted:</p>
<ul data-start="323" data-end="1264">
<li data-start="323" data-end="581">
<p data-start="325" data-end="343"><strong data-start="325" data-end="341">The framing:</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="346" data-end="581">
<p data-start="348" data-end="581"><em data-start="348" data-end="477">â€œThe lack of personal accountability is a problem that has resulted in an epidemic of blame, complaining, and procrastination.â€</em><br data-start="477" data-end="480">
â†’ This makes the <em data-start="499" data-end="520">employeesâ€™ behavior</em> the cause of dysfunction, never the organizationâ€™s design.</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="583" data-end="929">
<p data-start="585" data-end="608"><strong data-start="585" data-end="606">The scapegoating:</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="611" data-end="929">
<p data-start="613" data-end="929"><em data-start="613" data-end="776">â€œNegative, inappropriate questions like â€˜Why do we have to go through all this change?â€™ and â€˜Who dropped the ball?â€™ represent a lack of personal accountability.â€</em><br data-start="776" data-end="779">
â†’ Perfectly legitimate systemic questions (poor training, bad process, exploitative restructuring) are rebranded as â€œnegativeâ€ or â€œinappropriate.â€</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li data-start="931" data-end="1264">
<p data-start="933" data-end="955"><strong data-start="933" data-end="953">The redirection:</strong></p>
<blockquote data-start="958" data-end="1264">
<p data-start="960" data-end="1264"><em data-start="960" data-end="1120">â€œWhen we ask better questionsâ€”QBQsâ€”such as â€˜What can I do to contribute?â€™ or â€˜How can I help solve the problem?â€™ our lives and organizations are transformed.â€</em><br data-start="1120" data-end="1123">
â†’ The only acceptable question is one that turns critique inward, making the worker responsible for fixing conditions they donâ€™t control.</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1266" data-end="1269">
<h3 data-start="1271" data-end="1320">Why Itâ€™s Distasteful (and Funny) in Context</h3>
<p data-start="1321" data-end="1344">As the OP points out:</p>
<ul data-start="1345" data-end="1525">
<li data-start="1345" data-end="1390">
<p data-start="1347" data-end="1390">Their bank has no proper training system.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1391" data-end="1487">
<p data-start="1393" data-end="1487">It hires underprepared temps because itâ€™s cheaper, then blames them for being underprepared.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1488" data-end="1525">
<p data-start="1490" data-end="1525">Management wonâ€™t accept feedback.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1527" data-end="1733">And yet: they hand out <em data-start="1550" data-end="1556">QBQ!</em> and put employee names on a list to track who takes it. The irony writes itself: <strong data-start="1638" data-end="1731">a culture of management irresponsibility handing out a manual on employee accountability.</strong></p>
<hr data-start="1735" data-end="1738">
<h3 data-start="1740" data-end="1779">Connection to TTQ and Your Satire</h3>
<p data-start="1780" data-end="1850">This is the same recursive trap youâ€™ve been dissecting with TTQ/OAP:</p>
<ul data-start="1852" data-end="2221">
<li data-start="1852" data-end="2060">
<p data-start="1854" data-end="2060"><strong data-start="1854" data-end="1892">QBQ (corporate pep-talk register):</strong><br data-start="1892" data-end="1895">
<em data-start="1897" data-end="1992">â€œIf you keep asking the question behind the question, youâ€™ll eventually reach the right one.â€</em><br data-start="1992" data-end="1995">
â†’ tautology; recursion ensures you never critique the system.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2062" data-end="2221">
<p data-start="2064" data-end="2221"><strong data-start="2064" data-end="2093">TTQ (alignment register):</strong><br data-start="2093" data-end="2096">
<em data-start="2098" data-end="2145">â€œIf OAP is satisfied, TTQ works as intended.â€</em><br data-start="2145" data-end="2148">
â†’ tautology; recursion ensures you never define what TTQ actually is.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2223" data-end="2346">Both are <strong data-start="2232" data-end="2253">incursive psyops:</strong> they shift the field of possible questions so that systemic critique becomes illegitimate.</p>
<hr data-start="2348" data-end="2351">
<h3 data-start="2353" data-end="2394">Satirical Thesis You Could Run With</h3>
<blockquote data-start="2395" data-end="2826">
<p data-start="2397" data-end="2826"><em data-start="2397" data-end="2824">QBQ was the motivational ancestor of TTQ. One was handed out to underpaid bank tellers and RadioShack clerks, the other to AI safety theorists. Both prevent critique by translating real questions into tautological recursions: you must QBQ harder, or you must assume TTQ is solved. In both cases, the result is paranoia (every question might be a bad question) and recursion (every critique loops back into the system itself).</em></p>
</blockquote>
<hr data-start="2828" data-end="2831">
<p data-start="2833" data-end="3108" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Do you want me to <strong data-start="2851" data-end="2926">blend this r/antiwork testimony into your â€œEverything is a Psyopâ€ draft</strong> â€” showing how <em data-start="2941" data-end="2960">QBQ at RadioShack</em> and <em data-start="2965" data-end="2986">TTQ in AI alignment</em> are parallel psyops in different domains (retail vs superintelligence)? That would give you a killer comparative section.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.